  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Noble Supply and Logistics has $334M in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date. Noble Supply and Logistics received 106,729 awards this fiscal year to date, with an average award size of $3.1K. Obligations fell 65.3% year over year compared with the prior period. Fiscal obligations peaked earlier in the decade at $1.2B in FY24 before moving to $962M in FY25 and then to $334M in FY26. The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer for FY2026 to date, while the General Services Administration is the second-largest buyer. Noble Supply and Logistics does business across several manufacturing and wholesale markets, led by Service Establishment Equipment and Supplies Merchant Wholesalers and All Other Miscellaneous Manufacturing. Current-year totals are partial because FY2026 is fiscal year to date, and the note indicates award-value figures in tables are total contract values while the other figures are contract obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are Noble Supply and Logistics's biggest federal customers?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $300M in FY2026 to date. The General Services Administration is the second-largest buyer with $32.5M. The Department of State, Department of Homeland Security, and Department of Justice follow with $726K, $182K, and $162K respectively. The Department of Health and Human Services shows $0 for FY2026 to date."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What product and service markets does Noble Supply and Logistics serve?",
        "body": "Service Establishment Equipment and Supplies Merchant Wholesalers is the largest market for FY2026 to date at $107M. All Other Miscellaneous Manufacturing and Bolt, Nut, Screw, Rivet, and Washer Manufacturing are next with $83.3M and $51.5M. Other notable markets include Electrical Apparatus and Equipment, Wiring Supplies, and Related Equipment Merchant Wholesalers at $28.8M and Overhead Traveling Crane, Hoist, and Monorail System Manufacturing at $15.6M."
      }
    ]
  },
